   "reasoning": "The customer wants to change the order of items in a CMS collection and says the provided steps didn\u2019t work. The KB excerpts state the exact steps for manually reordering collection items and for mirroring that order to the live site, plus important constraints and app limitations. No fact only the customer holds is required to give a useful answer (we can provide the documented checklist and likely causes). This is not a request for a privileged action. All claims I will make are stated in the excerpts [8], [10], and the Wix app limitation in [1], so coverage is full.",
   "answer": "Try these documented steps and checks to reorder your CMS items (with the excerpts that state each step):\n\n1) Manually reorder items in the collection (desktop): Make sure the collection view\u2019s layout is set to Table, click the Reorder icon next to the item, then drag items up or down to set the order and repeat until done [8].\n\n2) Mirror that collection order on your live site (if you want the site to follow the collection order): In the collection, click Mirror on Site and enable the toggle \"Mirror item order on the site\" [8].\n\n3) Check for dataset sorts overriding the collection order: Any sort conditions added to datasets continue to override the order set in your collections, so if a dataset connected to the page has a sort, it will control the site order instead of the mirrored collection order [8][10].\n\n4) If you\u2019re using the Wix app: you can add, edit, duplicate, and delete items in the Wix app, but you cannot update the collection schema (layout/structure) from the app \u2014 do reordering and schema changes from the desktop if needed [1].\n\n5) CSV import behavior (if relevant): Imported CSV items are added to the top of the collection, which may change order after import [8].\n\nIf you\u2019ve followed the exact reorder + mirror steps above and it still doesn\u2019t work, tell me: whether you reordered in the collection (desktop) using Table + Reorder icon, whether you enabled \"Mirror on Site,\" and whether the page element is using a dataset with sorts \u2014 with those details I can point to the specific next check. Citations: [8], [10], [1].",
