   "reasoning": "The customer wants to know what to do to add a TXT record to verify their domain with Google Workspace when the domain is connected to Wix via pointing. The excerpts state the steps to get the TXT record from the Google Admin Console and that when a domain is connected via pointing the domain host (not Wix) controls DNS and must add TXT/DNS records. No customer-only fact is required to give this guidance (the ticket already states the domain is connected via pointing). A human does not need to act on the account \u2014 the customer must add the TXT at their domain host or contact that host for help.",
   "answer": "Because your domain is connected to Wix via pointing, Wix cannot manage your DNS \u2014 you must add the TXT record at your domain host (the registrar where you manage DNS). [1][7]\n\nSteps to follow:\n1) In the Google Admin Console, go to Domains and choose TXT verification to get the TXT record value to use. Copy the TXT record. [1][2]\n2) Sign in to your domain host (where the domain is pointed) and add a TXT record to the domain's DNS using the TXT value Google provided. (Wix cannot add this for you when the domain is connected via pointing.) [1][7]\n3) After adding the TXT record, return to the Google Admin Console and click Verify. If verification fails immediately, wait at least 10 minutes and try again (it may take a few tries). [1]\n\nIf you need help adding DNS records at your domain host, contact that domain host for assistance \u2014 instructions vary by host. [1][7]",
