   "reasoning": "The customer wants to know why the Connect PayPal option isn't available and how to link PayPal. The excerpts state the exact steps to connect PayPal and list a few reasons the option might not appear: wrong business location setting, PayPal being unsupported in certain countries (Russia), and that some payment providers or connections must be done from desktop (not iOS). All facts I would use to answer are present in the excerpts, and no fact only the customer holds is required to give a useful, documented troubleshooting checklist. A human is not required because this is a documentation/connection issue the customer can act on themselves.",
   "answer": "Try these documented checks and steps to reconnect PayPal [5]:\n\n1) Confirm you\u2019re in the right place and follow the Connect flow (desktop): Go to Accept Payments (or in some solutions, the Hotels tab for Wix Hotels) in your site\u2019s dashboard, then click Connect next to PayPal and follow the on\u2011screen sign\u2011in/authorization steps [5][1].\n\n2) Check your Business Location in the dashboard: PayPal availability depends on your business location\u2014make sure it\u2019s set correctly (top\u2011right of the Accept Payments page) and then try Connect again [5].\n\n3) Region restrictions: Wix no longer supports PayPal for businesses based in Russia (as of March 7, 2022). If your business location is set to Russia, the PayPal option will not be available [5].\n\n4) Use the correct interface if mobile: Some payment providers (and some setup actions) can only be completed from desktop. Connecting a payment method from the Wix mobile app is available only on Android; it\u2019s not possible on iOS. If you\u2019re on iOS, sign in from a desktop browser and try the Accept Payments > Connect flow [6].\n\n5) If you have multiple PayPal accounts: you can switch the connected PayPal account by entering the desired PayPal email in the Account information for the PayPal provider in Accept Payments and saving [10].\n\n6) If you\u2019re using Wix Hotels: If you\u2019re using the original Wix Hotels, payments are set up via the Hotels tab (Payments) and you must connect PayPal there; if you\u2019re using the new Hotels by HotelRunner the flow differs\u2014check which version you use and follow the matching article [1][5].\n\nIf you\u2019ve checked the business location, confirmed you\u2019re not in a restricted country, tried from a desktop browser, and still don\u2019t see Connect next to PayPal, please tell me (a) the exact business location shown in your dashboard and (b) whether you\u2019re on desktop or mobile and which interface (site dashboard Accept Payments or Hotels tab) you\u2019re using\u2014I\u2019ll guide you to the next steps. (These details will let us pinpoint the remaining possibilities.) [5][6][1][10]",
   "v4_decision": "RESOLVE",
   "reference_answer": "There are 2 main reasons for payment providers not appearing in the Accept Payments tab:\n  \n  1. Different payment providers are available in different locations. PayPal is available in around 200 countries. Please check the following link to make sure PayPal is available in your location: [visit PayPal] (https://www.paypal.com/pn/webapps/mpp/country-worldwide).\n  \n  \n  2. If you began onboarding with Wix Payments, you may have selected a prohibited product or service. If so, this may remove the option to onboard with other payment providers who prohibit similar items. \n  \n  For more information, please see [our checklist for restricted products & services when setting up your payments] (https://support.wix.com/en/article/checking-for-restricted-products-services-when-setting-up-your-payments).\n  \n  If you mistakenly completed a CBD declaration, or selected a restricted product/service, please contact [Wix Customer Care] (https://www.wix.com/contact).",
