   "reasoning": "The customer says they created pages in the Editor, published, the pages are not hidden, and the pages are published but not appearing live. They want those pages to appear on the live site. The excerpts collectively state the checks and causes that explain why editor changes may not appear live (publish vs save, browser/cache issues, site history overwritten, header/footer/menu layout, domain/plan/DNS issues). Nothing the customer uniquely holds is required to give a useful troubleshooting checklist (we do not need their site name or account details to list the documented checks). No human action on their account is required \u2014 these are self-service checks documented in the KB. Therefore we can RESOLVE using the documented steps and cite the relevant excerpts that state each point.",
   "answer": "Question: Why are pages I created in the Editor not appearing on my live site even though I clicked Publish? Answer: Follow these documented checks (each line cites the article that states it):\n\n- Make sure you actually clicked Publish (Save does not make changes live); after publishing click View Site to check the live site [2].\n- If you did publish but still see differences, clear your browser cache and make sure you\u2019re using a supported, up-to-date browser \u2014 outdated cache or browser rendering can cause editor/live differences [1].\n- Check Site History in the editor in case a collaborator saved over your changes; you can restore the last saved version that contains the pages or content [1].\n- If the pages are part of a menu and the menu is missing on the live site, confirm the menu is added, the page\u2019s layout is set to Standard (not hidden), the header/footer isn\u2019t hidden or frozen, and then publish and refresh your live site [5].\n- If your site uses a custom domain, verify the site is published to the correct site and domain, your domain and plan are active, and DNS/propagation is complete (domain connection issues or expired plan can prevent pages from appearing) [9].\n- If you have custom code, consider disabling it temporarily \u2014 custom code can cause unexpected live-site behavior [1].\n\nIf you complete these steps and the pages still don\u2019t appear, tell us: (1) whether the pages are visible in Preview mode in the editor, (2) whether you can view them using the editor\u2019s View Site link, and (3) whether your site uses a custom domain or the free wixsite URL \u2014 with that info we can recommend the next step.",
