   "policy_override": null,
   "reasoning": "The customer wants to know why they haven't received a payment in their bank account. The excerpts include documentation about payout management, reasons for declined payments, verification timing, SEPA timing, and where payouts are handled, so they STATE the facts needed to give general troubleshooting steps and next actions. Nothing the customer alone knows (which specific payout, which payment provider or payment ID, the payment status shown in their Payments table) is required to give a useful, actionable checklist \u2014 we can list documented causes and what to check next. The customer is not asking us to act on their account or to look up their records, so this does not require human authority.",
   "answer": "I\u2019m sorry the payment hasn\u2019t reached your bank yet. Here are the documented checks and next steps you can do now: 1) Check which payment provider handled the payout \u2014 if you use a third\u2011party provider (Stripe, PaidBy Bank, PayU, etc.) payouts are managed by that provider, so contact them for payout timing and specifics [10][1]. 2) If you use Wix Payments, open your Payments table in your dashboard and check the transaction or payout status (e.g. Pending, Failed, Returned). The Payments table explains what each status means and what to do next (for example, Returned means the payout was returned by your bank) [5]. 3) If your Wix Payments account is still being verified, verification can take up to 7 business days; if more than 7 business days passed and your info is correct, contact Wix Customer Care for an investigation [6]. 4) If the payment was made via SEPA or was saved as a SEPA payment method, note that SEPA confirmations can take up to 7 business days to arrive and refunds (if applicable) up to 20 business days; check the SEPA article for pending/declined reasons and timing [9]. 5) If transactions are being declined, consult the decline reasons and suggested actions (currency mismatch, blocked/restricted provider account, 3\u2011D Secure failures, insufficient funds, unsupported currency) and act accordingly \u2014 for provider account issues contact the payment provider; for currency mismatches you may need to change provider or currency settings [2][1]. 6) If you\u2019re unsure which provider processed the payout or you checked the above and still can\u2019t find the payout, tell me: (a) whether you use Wix Payments or a third\u2011party provider, and (b) the payment date and amount shown in your site\u2019s Payments table (or a screenshot of the status). With those details I can point you to the exact next step or, if it\u2019s a Wix Payments verification exceeding 7 business days, advise opening a Customer Care investigation [6][5].",
   "v4_decision": "RESOLVE",
   "reference_answer": "If you have not received your payment in your bank account yet, there are several steps you can take to troubleshoot the issue:\n\n1. **Check Verification Status**: Ensure that your Wix Payments account is successfully verified. Incomplete verification can delay payouts. You can learn more about the verification process [here](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-payments-verification-process).\n\n2. **Review Bank Details**: Verify that the bank details associated with your Wix Payments account are correct. Incorrect bank details can cause payouts to fail. You can update your bank details by following the steps outlined [here](https://support.wix.com/en/article/failed-payout-in-wix-payments).\n\n3. **Check Payout Schedule**: Confirm your payout schedule (daily, weekly, or monthly) and allow 3-5 business days for the funds to appear in your bank account after the payout is sent. More information on payout schedules can be found [here](https://support.wix.com/en/article/changing-your-wix-payments-payout-schedule).\n\n4. **Look for Failed Payouts**: Check your Wix Payments dashboard for any failed payouts. If a payout has failed, it will be marked as 'Failed' and placed on hold until the issue is resolved. Instructions for resolving failed payouts are available [here](https://support.wix.com/en/article/failed-payout-in-wix-payments).\n\n5. **Payouts on Hold**: If there is an issue blocking your payout, it may be on hold. You can view the reason for the hold and instructions for resolving it in your Wix Payments dashboard. More information on payouts on hold can be found [here](https://support.wix.com/en/article/payouts-on-hold).\n\nIf you have checked all the above and still have not received your payment, consider reaching out to Wix support for further assistance.",
