   "answer": "Question: What additional information might Wix require to verify my business Wix Payments account? Answer: Wix may require you to provide several documents and correct account details to complete verification: - General requirements and timing: Wix verifies the information you submit after the first successful payment; verification can take up to 7 business days, and you have 30 days from the first transaction to complete setup before suspension occurs ([2], [3]). If verification isn\u2019t completed in time, the account can be suspended and payments refunded ([2], [3]). - Identity and business documents: For business accounts you\u2019ll be asked to upload a valid government-issued photo ID and a bank statement (or other bank document) to the Wix Payments Dashboard ([2], [6], [7]). Photo ID must be a clear, color, non-expired passport, driver\u2019s license, or government ID meeting the listed image and content rules ([6]). - Bank/account documents: Provide a bank statement, a voided check, or an official bank letter showing the full account number, bank logo, account holder name, and issued within the specified timeframe (bank statement/letter issued within the last 12 months) ([7]). - Company documents and matching data: The country where your company is registered and the country of your company\u2019s bank must match the country you select for setup; company name, tax ID (e.g. codice fiscale / UTR where applicable) and business/legal names must match the documents and what you entered during setup. Mismatches can cause verification failure and payouts to be put on hold ([2], [1], [5], [9]). - Address verification: Upload a recent address verification document (e.g. utility bill) dated within the last 6 months, with the full name and address visible. PO Boxes are not accepted ([1], [6], [9]). - File requirements and formats: Documents must be clear, show full pages/corners, not be screenshots, and be in an accepted format (HEIC, JPEG, JPG, PDF, PNG); file size limits apply. Follow the guidelines to avoid rejection ([6], [7]). - If information changes or you update details: Editing account settings triggers re-verification; during re-verification your status temporarily becomes Accepting Payments but payouts remain on hold until verification completes (which can take up to 7 business days) ([4]). - If verification fails or you think details are incorrect: The KB states that mismatched information causes verification failure and payouts to be held; if the required time has passed after submitting correct info, contact Wix Customer Care to investigate ([5], [1], [3]). What you should do next: 1) Check Accept Payments > Wix Payments in your dashboard and click Complete Setup / Complete Account Setup to see what specific documents Wix is requesting for your business account ([3]). 2) Prepare and upload the requested documents following the guidelines above (photo ID, bank statement/voided check/bank letter, address proof, company/tax documents where applicable) ([6], [7], [1]). 3) If you already uploaded the documents and more than 7 business days have passed since submission (or 30 days since your first transaction) and your account is still not verified, contact Wix Customer Care for investigation ([1], [2], [3]).",
