   "answer": "To add a personalized name to your automated emails, add a dynamic/personalized value (e.g. contact first name) to the subject or body and set fallback text. Steps: 1) Open the automation/email template and click Edit for the subject or the relevant text field. [1][7] 2) In the subject: click +Personalize or + Dynamic Value below the subject and pick the contact-first-name (or similar) value from the dropdown; in the body: click + Add Personalized Content / + Add Dynamic Value and choose the name variable. [1][7] 3) Enter fallback text (for example \u201cvalued customer\u201d) to display when the recipient\u2019s name isn\u2019t available. [1][2][7] 4) Save/Publish the changes (Save & Continue / Publish or Update). [1][7] 5) (Optional) Preview and send a test email to check the result. [1][7] Note: selecting dynamic values from the variable list is available on desktop only. [2]",
