   "answer": "You can add a subscribe form yourself \u2014 here are the documented ways and a few settings to consider.\n\n1) In the Wix Editor / Studio Editor:\n- In the editor click Add Elements (Add), choose Contact & Forms, scroll to the Subscribe section and drag a Subscribe form onto your page. Then click the form, choose Edit Form / Form Settings to customize it and Save/Publish [2][4].\n\n2) In Wix ADI:\n- Click Add in the ADI top bar. Choose Section to Page > Subscribe (or add a Contact page and select a contact layout). You can also add a subscribe form to the footer so it appears on all pages by editing the footer and checking Subscribe [1].\n\n3) After adding the form \u2014 useful settings:\n- New subscribers are automatically added to your Contacts with a 'Subscriber' label [2][6].\n- You can enable Subscriber double opt-in so subscribers must verify their email before being added (recommended for explicit consent) [2][7].\n- You can customize layout, design, email notification recipients, submission limits, and autofill behavior in the form settings [2].\n\n4) Want the subscribe form to notify readers of new blog posts?\n- After adding the subscribe form you can set your blog to send email notifications to subscribers when you publish a post; blog notifications are managed via Automations in your site's dashboard [4][9].\n\nIf you tell me whether you\u2019re using ADI or the Editor I can highlight the exact click path for that interface (both methods above are valid) and list the key toggles to check in Form Settings.",
