   "answer": "The Right Click Protect App prevents visitors from downloading content via right\u2011click by showing a customizable copyright message when they right\u2011click protected elements. You can add it from the Wix App Market (Add Apps / App Market \u2192 search for Right Click Protect \u2192 Add to Site) and edit its Settings and Design (message text, theme, font, color) in the editor [1][8]. Important limitations to know: it cannot currently restrict protection to specific pages (the app applies site\u2011wide) [1][10]; it does not block visitors from selecting text and using Ctrl+C to copy (this is not protected) [2][3][8]; right\u2011click protection is not supported on mobile devices (mobile users may still save images via long\u2011tap) [3][6][8]; it does not provide 100% protection\u2014visitors can still use print screen or access source code if they know how [3][4]; and it does not protect content inside third\u2011party apps or embedded HTML (those remain unprotected if the third\u2011party allows downloads) [3][4][8]. Alternatives and complements: use a Wix Pro Gallery (has built\u2011in right\u2011click protection for gallery images) or add watermarks to images via Photo Studio or Photo Albums to deter copying [5][8]. If you want to remove the app later, select it in the editor and delete it, then publish your site to save the change [1]. If you\u2019d like, I can point you to the exact editor steps for your editor view (Editor, Studio, or other) \u2014 otherwise follow the Add Apps/App Market steps above to install and customize it [1][8].",
