   "answer": "You can refund a recurring payment made through Wix Payments from your site\u2019s Payments page. On desktop (or in the Wix app) go to Payments in your site's dashboard, click the specific payment, click Refund, enter the amount (you can do a full or partial refund) and confirm. Refunds issued through Wix Payments typically take 3\u20135 business days to reach the customer\u2019s card/bank account. Refunds cannot be canceled once initiated. [2][4][8]\n\nIf your Wix Payments balance is insufficient to cover the refund, you can add funds and complete the refund from the Payments page by choosing Add Funds & Complete Refund and entering card details; once the funds are processed, Wix will automatically issue the refund. [6]\n\nIf the recurring payment was for a pricing plan/subscription, you can also cancel the subscription from My Subscriptions, and then issue the refund for the payment via Payments as above. [4]\n\nIf you follow these steps and the refund option does not appear for that payment, or the payment was not processed through Wix Payments, you'll need to issue the refund directly through the payment provider that processed the transaction. [1][3][5]\n\nIf you\u2019d like, reply with whether the payment was processed via Wix Payments and whether you see the payment in Payments; I can then point to the exact place in the dashboard to click. [2]",
