   "answer": "If you\u2019re a sole trader in the UK, the KB recommends the UK sole proprietor account only if you can meet the UK-specific requirements \u2014 specifically, submit a Unique Taxpayer Reference (UTR) number and use a business bank account (not a personal bank account). If you have those (and the other verification items like ID, physical address and supporting documents), choose the UK sole proprietor/business account [2][3]. If you haven\u2019t registered for a UTR or you only have a personal bank account, choose an Individual account instead (you can switch later once you have the UTR/business bank account) [2][3]. Note: the verification process can take up to 7 business days after you submit the required documents, and there are time limits for completing setup (if not completed in 30 days the Wix Payments account may be suspended; after 60 days payments processed may be refunded) \u2014 be sure to upload your ID, bank statement and any tax documents when prompted [5].",
