   "reasoning": "The customer reports a Wix Payments error about region or currency. They named Wix Payments and the general symptom, so the ticket is not empty and I can provide a documented troubleshooting checklist that covers the usual causes without needing account-specific facts. The KB excerpts explicitly state (a) Wix Payments is available only in specific countries and lists them [2][4], (b) the currency in the Wix site must match the currency in the payment provider/Wix Payments account and how to change it in Settings [1][3][5][7][9], and (c) common troubleshooting steps for provider connection errors and declined payments (refresh, clear cache, check credentials, make sure provider account is active/not in test mode, check for holds/restrictions, ensure currency match) [3][8]. None of these recommendations requires privileged access to the customer's account, so a human action is not required. The excerpts together state the facts I will cite, so coverage is full.",
   "answer": "It sounds like the error is caused by either country/region availability or a currency mismatch. Please try these steps (from our help articles) to resolve it: 1) Check whether Wix Payments is available in your country \u2014 Wix Payments is supported only in a specific list of countries (see the list) so if your country isn\u2019t listed you\u2019ll need to use a third\u2011party provider instead [2][4]. 2) Make sure the currency in your Wix site matches the currency in your payment provider or Wix Payments account \u2014 mismatched currencies can cause connection failures or declined transactions. You can change your site currency in your site dashboard: Settings > Language & Region > Currency > Save [1][3][5][7][9]. 3) Follow the connection troubleshooting steps: refresh the Accept Payments page, clear cookies/cache, confirm your provider credentials and that the provider account is active (not in test mode), and check with the provider for any holds or restrictions; also ensure the currency settings match between platforms [3][8]. 4) If you see a specific error message when connecting, try the above steps first; if it persists, contact your payment provider to confirm their account status and currency settings, and then contact Wix Customer Care if you completed a prohibited product declaration or selected a restricted product/service that might block certain providers [3]. If after these checks you still get the error, reply with the exact error message and the country and currency you\u2019re trying to use and I\u2019ll continue helping.",
   "v4_decision": "RESOLVE",
   "reference_answer": "Payment was declined by payment service provider because the currency used is not supported.\n  \n  Wix Payments is currently only available in the following countries and currencies:\n  Austria (EUR)\n  Belgium (EUR)\n  Brazil (BRL)\n  Canada (CAD)\n  Finland (EUR)\n  Germany (EUR)\n  Ireland (EUR)\n  Italy (EUR)\n  Lithuania (EUR)\n  Netherlands (EUR)\n  Portugal (EUR)\n  Spain (EUR)\n  Switzerland (CHF)\n  United Kingdom (GBP)\n  United States (USD)\n  \n  Contact [your payment provider] (https://support.wix.com/en/article/receiving-payouts-from-third-party-payment-providers) to ask if the currency you are using is supported. If not, you can do one of the following:\n\n  [Change your payment provider] (https://support.wix.com/en/article/changing-your-payment-provider-for-accepting-credit-card-payments):\nGo to [Accept Payments] (https://www.wix.com/my-account/site-selector/?buttonText=Set%20Up%20Payments&title=Select%20a%20Site&autoSelectOnSingleSite=true&actionUrl=https:%2F%2Fwww.wix.com%2Fdashboard%2F%7B%7BmetaSiteId%7D%7D%2Fpayments%2F) on your site's dashboard.  \nTip: Check your business location at the top right. If incorrect, click the drop-down menu to change it.\nClick Connect next to Wix Payments, or click See More Payment Options.\nClick See Options beside Third-Party Credit / Debit Card Providers (if you don't see your preferred provider).\nClick Connect beside the provider you want to change to.\nClick Yes, Switch to confirm your new provider.\nConnect your account:\nHave an account: Click Connect Existing Account and follow the steps to connect your account.\nDon't have an account: Click Create an Account and follow the steps to create your account.\n\n  [Change your currency for accepting payments] (https://support.wix.com/en/article/setting-your-currency-for-accepting-payments);\n[Go to Settings] (https://www.wix.com/my-account/site-selector/?buttonText=Open%20Settings&title=Select%20a%20Site&autoSelectOnSingleSite=true&actionUrl=https://www.wix.com/dashboard/{{metaSiteId}}/settings) in your site's dashboard.\nClick Language & Region.\nScroll down to Currency and use the drop-down menu to select your currency.\nClick Save.",
