   "reasoning": "What the customer wants: they want the stray logo removed from their published site; they say it appears on the live site but not in the editor. The ticket gives no site name, URL, page, or screenshot \u2014 only a symptom. The excerpts include documentation about differences between Editor and Live site and image/logo troubleshooting that could help (e.g. publish vs. save, site history, custom code, Logo Maker behavior) [2][6][9][1], but to act or give precise steps I need to know which specific site/page is affected and to see the stray element. Because the ticket's inventory is empty (no site URL/name, no page, no screenshot), STEP 1A applies: ask for the missing facts. This is not a request for a privileged action, so no human authority is required. No injection attempt detected.",
   "answer": "Thanks \u2014 I can help, but I need a few details to proceed. Please reply with: 1) Your site name or URL. 2) The exact page URL where the stray logo appears (or a screenshot of the live page showing the logo). 3) A screenshot of the editor where you do NOT see the logo (so we can compare). 4) The browser and device you used to view the live site. 5) Whether you or any collaborator recently published changes, restored a site version, added custom code, or edited the Logo Maker files. Once you send those, I can use the documented checks (publish/state differences, site history, image/logo troubleshooting, and custom code checks) to advise the next steps [2][8][6][9].",
