   "answer": "Here are the relevant collection and store limits as documented: \n\n- Free site CMS collection item quotas: free sites in a Wix Studio account have a 10,000 collection-item quota; free sites not in Wix Studio (or after leaving Studio) have a 1,000 collection-item quota [1].\n\n- The 10,000 limit applies only to collections you create and does not include collections created by Wix apps [5].\n\n- If your site\u2019s plan includes higher CMS limits (for example Business Elite / Elite Premium), those plans allow up to 500,000 collection items; custom CMS quotas are available for Business Elite or Elite Premium sites by contacting sales [9].\n\n- If your site\u2019s plan has a lower CMS limit than your current item count, existing items are not deleted but you won\u2019t be able to add more until you delete items or upgrade to a plan with a higher quota [8].\n\n- Separately, Wix Stores product limits (shop-specific) include up to 50,000 products uploaded via the Stores dashboard or CSV; other store limits (options, choices, variants) are documented too (e.g. up to 6 product options per product, up to 100 choices per option, up to 1,000 variants per product) [2].\n\nIf you want, tell me whether you mean CMS collection items (site collections) or store product limits and which plan or site type you have, and I can point to the exact quota that applies to your site.",
