   "answer": "You can create an automation for a standard Wix form from your site's dashboard. Steps: 1) Go to Automations in your site's dashboard and click + New Automation, then + Start from Scratch or choose a suggested automation [7]. 2) Give the automation a name, then in the Trigger section choose Wix Forms as the trigger (note: you may see two Wix Forms trigger options \u2014 the blue icon for new Wix Forms and the red icon for old Wix Forms) [1][3]. 3) Select which form(s) will trigger the automation: choose Any (all forms) or Specific and pick the form(s) you want [1][3]. 4) Set the trigger frequency under Limit frequency (Don't limit, Once per contact, or Once per contact every 24 hrs) and optionally add a delay or conditions if needed [1][3]. 5) Choose an action for the automation (for example, send an automated email, create a task, send data to Google Sheets, run Velo code, etc.) and configure that action [7][1]. 6) Review timing and action settings, then Activate the automation [5][7]. If you want to send automated emails after form submissions, make sure your form includes an email field before choosing the send-email action [3].",
   "v4_decision": "RESOLVE",
   "reference_answer": "To create an automation for your form:\n\n1. Go to Automations in your site's dashboard.\n2. Click + New Automation.\n3. Click + Start from Scratch.\n4. Click the title to give your automation a name.\n5. In the Trigger section, click Wix Forms (blue icon).\n6. Select an option under Select a trigger:\n   - Option chosen on a form: The automation is triggered when a specific option within a form is chosen before being submitted.\n   - Form submitted: The automation is triggered after a form on your site is submitted.\n7. Choose the relevant option under Select which forms trigger this automation:\n   - Any: All forms trigger this automation.\n   - Specific: Select which form(s) will trigger this automation.\n8. Click the Limit frequency to drop-down to set trigger frequency:\n   - Don't limit (trigger every time): Your action will take place every time it is triggered.\n   - Once per contact: Your action will take place only once per contact.\n   - Once per contact every 24hrs: Your action will take place only once per contact in any 24hr period.\n9. (Optional) Add a delay between a trigger and its action, to have the action occur after a certain amount of time passes.\n10. (Optional) Add a condition to make the automation occur when certain conditions are met.\n11. Choose an action and decide how you want to respond to the trigger. For example, send an email, a chat message, or a push notification.\n12. (Optional) Add a chain of follow-up actions from the initial action.\n13. Click Activate to save and activate the automation.",
