   "answer": "How can I customize the content in automated emails for Wix Bookings (confirmation, cancellation and reminders for users)?\n\nYou can customize Wix Bookings automated emails from your site's dashboard. Summary of the steps and important notes:\n\n1) Open the Email controls in Booking Settings: Go to Booking Settings in your site's dashboard, then click Emails & SMS notifications to see the list of booking email automations [1][4].\n\n2) Edit an automation: Hover over the automation you want to customize and click Edit next to it. For reminder emails you can also click Edit next to Timing to adjust when the reminder is sent [2].\n\n3) Manage sender and reply-to: Under Manage details (click Edit under Manage details, then the More Actions icon \u2192 Edit) you can change the Sender's name and the Reply\u2011to email address that appears when clients reply [2]. Note the guidance about using an authenticated business email instead of a public Gmail/Yahoo address to avoid spam folders [2].\n\n4) Edit the email template content and layout: Click Edit under Create an email to edit the template. You can customize existing elements, add more elements (text, images, videos), and (optionally) Switch Template to choose a different style (switching templates will replace existing changes) [2][1]. Some parts of the pre-installed automations cannot be changed to ensure delivery of important session information [1].\n\n5) Attachments and calendar invites: For Confirmation and Cancellation automations you can select the Calendar invite (ICS) checkbox to include an ICS file with booking details; note ICS may not work properly for some Microsoft Outlook recipients and cannot be sent for courses [2].\n\n6) Use variables/dynamic values (Hotels / HotelRunner): If you use Wix Hotels by HotelRunner, you can add dynamic values (variables) into subject and body and choose from Property, Customer, or Reservation variables; the same article shows editing and sending test emails for preview [3][5].\n\n7) Alternative: Wix Automations for custom booking emails: If you prefer more customization or need to include video conferencing links in a custom automated email, you can create Automations (Automations \u2192 + New Automation \u2192 Wix Bookings \u2192 Session booked \u2192 Send an email \u2192 Edit Template). Disabling the default confirmation and using Automations is a documented option in some workflows to manage how video conferencing links are delivered [9][4]. Also, Wix announced you can now customize outgoing confirmation, cancellation and reminder email content and add attachments (see the Bookings Request note) [6].\n\nSave your changes when done. If you want guidance for a specific email type (confirmation vs reminder vs cancellation) or for using variables in a particular template, tell me which one and I can give the exact steps for that automation [1][2][4][3][5][6].",
