   "answer": "You can offer free shipping above a set order amount in two ways \u2014 enable free shipping in a shipping rule, or create a free-shipping coupon. 1) Enable free shipping in a shipping rule: create or edit a shipping rule (Flat Rate, Rate by Product, Rate by Order Price, or Rate by Weight), and check the \"Offer free shipping when customer buys over a certain amount\" box, then enter the threshold amount and save. (See Flat Rate and shipping-rule instructions: [4], rate-by-product and advanced settings: [2], rate-by-order-price in the app: [6], and the general shipping-rule example: [1].) 2) Create a Free Shipping coupon: go to Coupons in your dashboard, click +New Coupon, choose Free Shipping, enter the coupon code/name, select \"Minimum order subtotal\" under Apply to and enter the minimum amount, then Create Coupon. This applies the coupon only when the subtotal meets the threshold. (See coupon creation: [8].) Choose the method you prefer: shipping-rule free shipping applies automatically at checkout when the order meets the amount; the coupon requires customers to enter or apply the coupon code (or be given it).",
