   "reasoning": "The customer wants guidance for setting up Meta Pixel event tracking for Wix Bookings (a documentation/how-to request). The excerpts state which booking events Wix sends to Meta/Google Analytics and how to connect the Meta Pixel & CAPI integration. Required facts (what events are tracked; how to connect the integration; prerequisites) are present in the excerpts. No fact only the customer holds is required to give the documented steps. This does not require any privileged action on the customer's account. Therefore I can resolve by giving step-by-step guidance and citing the excerpts.",
   "answer": "You can track Wix Bookings events with the Meta Pixel by connecting the Meta Pixel & CAPI integration and then using the built-in booking events Wix automatically sends. Steps: 1) Make sure your site meets the prerequisites: upgrade your site and connect a domain before using Marketing Integrations ([8], [10]). 2) Connect Meta Pixel & CAPI: In your site's dashboard go to Marketing Integrations \u2192 click Connect under Meta Pixel & CAPI \u2192 Connect to Facebook \u2192 choose your profile and sign in \u2192 follow the permission prompts and click Done. Once connected you should start seeing data in your Facebook Business Manager (Events Manager) ([8]). 3) The booking-related events Wix automatically sends to Meta are: View Content (when a visitor views a service page), Initiate Checkout (when a visitor clicks the Book Now button), Select Date (after the user selects a date), Add Payment Info (after the visitor adds payment info), and Purchase (when a visitor books and reaches the Thank-you page) \u2014 use these events in Ads Manager/Events Manager to track service views and bookings ([1]). 4) If you use Facebook Ads with Wix, note Wix may automatically connect your site to Meta Pixel & CAPI when creating dynamic campaigns; disconnecting can affect campaigns and may not be possible if a campaign exists ([4]). 5) After connecting, view event data in Facebook Business Manager \u2192 Events Manager (or Ads Manager) to confirm events are arriving; if data is missing or incorrect, follow the troubleshooting guidance in the Meta Pixel & CAPI article ([8]) and check Events Manager in your Facebook account ([1]).",
   "v4_decision": "RESOLVE",
   "reference_answer": "Wix automatically sends events to Facebook about your Wix Bookings services on your site. Using the Meta pixel, you can track events on your site such as views and purchases for each service you offer. \n\nThe events you see in your Facebook account are:\nView Content: When a visitor views a service page.\nInitiate Checkout: When a visitor clicks on the \"Book Now\" button.\nSelect Date: After the user selects a date for his service.\nAdd Payment Info: After the visitor added his payment information.\nPurchase: When a visitor books a service and is taken to the \"Thank-you\" page.\n\nTo connect your site:\n1. Go to [Marketing Integrations] (https://manage.wix.com/my-account/site-selector/?siteType=HtmlWeb&actionUrl=https:%2F%2Fwww.wix.com%2Fdashboard%2F%7B%7BmetaSiteId%7D%7D%2Fmarketing-integration%3FreferralInfo%3Dmarketing_integrations_article_link&title=Marketing%20Integrations&buttonText=Add%20Integrations) in your site's dashboard. \n2. Click Connect under Meta Pixel & CAPI.\n3. Click Connect to Facebook.\n4. (If required) Choose your profile in the pop-up and sign in.\n5. Click Next.\n6. Click Next to grant the necessary permissions to Wix Marketing Tools.\n7. Click Next.\n8. Click Next on the What is Wix Marketing Tools allowed to do? page.\n9. Click Done. \n\nTo see the event data in Facebook:\n1. Sign into your Facebook account. \n2. Click Ads Manager, located in the top left corner. \n3. Click Events Manager.",
