   "answer": "Here are steps you can follow in the Editor to locate the overlapping item and remove the Google Maps element from the footer: 1) Use the Layers panel to find and select the map: open the Layers panel (bottom left/bottom of the editor) and pick the element from Header / Page / Footer [2][1]. 2) Use the Overlapping Items entry in the element's right\u2011click menu to select elements that are covering the map: right\u2011click an area, hover Overlapping Items and pick the map or the covering element [2]. 3) Toggle through page elements if you still can\u2019t find it: press Ctrl (Cmd on Mac) + Shift + M to cycle forward (Ctrl/Cmd + M to cycle backwards) until the map is selected [1][2]. 4) If the footer is frozen and covering the map, check the footer Settings and disable Freeze or resize the footer so it no longer overlaps the map [3]. 5) To remove the map from the footer so it\u2019s no longer part of the footer: drag the element away from the footer onto another area of the page (this detaches it from the footer) or select the element and press Delete to remove it from the site entirely [5][10]. 6) If another element is covering the map after selecting it, use Arrange \u2192 Bring to Front or Move Backward on the covering element (right\u2011click \u2192 Arrange) to make the map accessible [1][3]. If you try these steps and still cannot access or remove the map, please reply and tell me which step failed and what you see (e.g., you cannot select the footer at all, or the Overlapping Items list is empty) so I can advise next steps.",
