   "answer": "You can customize the Cart page for mobile from your editor. Steps: 1) Open your site editor and go to the Cart page (how to access it depends on which business solution you use \u2014 Wix Stores, Bookings, Restaurants \u2014 see the options under Pages & Menu / Cart & Thank You) [2]. 2) Switch to the mobile editor (click the Switch to Mobile / Switch to Tablet / Mobile icon at the top) so you\u2019re editing the mobile breakpoint [1][8]. 3) Click the Cart Page element and choose Settings. Use the Settings tab to choose which elements to show on the Cart page (promo code link, Add a note, shipping & delivery rates, Show link / Continue Shopping, express checkout buttons) [5][2]. 4) Use the Design tab to change background, borders, fonts, button styles and the appearance of payment/express checkout buttons [1][5]. 5) Use the Text tab to edit the Cart page text (checkout button label, instructional text, disclaimers, and you can add a short message under the total up to 90 characters) [1][5]. 6) Mobile-specific controls: decide where to display the checkout button for mobile (options include bottom-only or both top and bottom in some editors) and note that in some Studio Editor variants it\u2019s not possible to select checkout-button placement; many mobile customizations don\u2019t affect desktop and vice versa, so switch breakpoints as needed while editing [1][8]. 7) If you use a side cart, you can customize its mobile behavior and whether clicking outside closes it, and customize the page overlay when the side cart is shown \u2014 these settings are available in the side cart settings in the editor [9]. If you tell me which editor interface you\u2019re using (Wix Editor, Studio Editor, or ADI) I can include any tiny variations in the steps, but the steps above cover the documented mobile Cart customization options [1][2][5][9][8].",
