   "reasoning": "The customer asks why their payout was delayed. This is a documentation question that the KB covers: the excerpts state the typical processing and payout timelines, verification and account-status requirements, reasons payouts are put on hold, reserve funds, grouping/threshold rules, and where to see the specific hold reason. No account-only fact is required to give a useful, general answer (we can list documented causes and show where to check). A human action is not required because the customer is asking for explanations and checks they can perform themselves. The excerpts together fully state the documented causes and instructions to check the payout reason, so we can RESOLVE from the KB.",
   "answer": "Here are the documented reasons a payout can be delayed and what to check: \n\n- Account verification and Active status: Your first payout (and any payouts) requires a successfully verified/Active Wix Payments account; incomplete verification can delay your first payout [1][2][9].\n- Processing and pending periods: After a customer pays, payments go through processing/settlement and a pending period (usually 2\u20135 business days) before being added to a scheduled payout; this can make payouts appear delayed while payments are still settling [2][1].\n- Scheduled payout timing and bank transit: Once sent, payouts can take 3\u20135 business days to reach your bank; you can also choose daily/weekly/monthly schedules which affect timing [1][2].\n- Payouts grouped by payment method or thresholds: If you have grouped payment methods payouts may be scheduled by group; in some products (Wix Studio) payouts wait until earnings meet a threshold (e.g. $200) before a payout is created, which can make it look delayed until the threshold is met [2][3].\n- Payouts on hold reasons: Payouts are placed on hold for issues such as a failed payout or an unresolved verification problem; the held amount includes any other available funds blocked by the issue [9].\n- Reserve funds: Wix may hold a rolling or one-time reserve from payouts (held for a set time) to cover refunds/chargebacks; reserve amounts are released later and then added to your next scheduled payout, which can affect what is sent [10].\n- Transaction status details: The payments/payouts table shows statuses (e.g. Pending, Successful, Paid Out, Payout Reversed) that explain whether funds are still processing or were returned/held [6].\n\nWhat to do now (where to check):\n- Open the Payouts area in your Wix Payments dashboard and click the specific payout to see the reason for the failure or hold and follow the on-screen instructions [1][9].\n- Verify your Wix Payments account and payout settings (bank details, schedule) if verification or incorrect details are flagged [1][2][3].\n- If the payout status hasn\u2019t updated after the expected windows (processing + bank transit) and you\u2019ve confirmed verification and details, contact Wix Customer Care as suggested in the Studio article if applicable [3].\n\nIf you want, tell me what status you see in your Payouts area (the status text or a screenshot) and I can point to the exact next step from the KB.",
